Day 4 – Conditional Statements

Full Stack Web Development with Java Internship

Today’s lecture focused on conditional statements in Java. The mentor explained how decision-making is implemented in programs using different conditional constructs.

🔹 Topics Covered
1️⃣ if Statement

Used to execute a block of code when a specified condition is true.

2️⃣ if-else Statement

Used to execute one block of code if the condition is true and another block if the condition is false.

3️⃣ else-if Ladder

Used when multiple conditions need to be checked sequentially.

4️⃣ switch Statement

Used when multiple cases depend on a single variable. It improves readability compared to multiple if-else conditions.

🔹 Key Concepts Learned

How conditions are evaluated using relational operators (>, <, ==, !=).

Use of logical operators (&&, ||, !) to combine multiple conditions.

Importance of break statement in switch-case.

Flow of execution in decision-making structures.

🎯 Learning Outcome

Understood how programs make decisions.

Learned to implement logic-based conditions.

Improved understanding of control flow in Java.